{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788174376557,"sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a0577f9c2e7ca18dd0427ec2364f59","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat docs/director/ART-BIBLE.md 2>&1; echo \"==WORLD_BIBLE==\"; cat tools/builders/generate_world_visual_foundation.py 2>&1 | head -n 100"},"output":"# THE OUTSKIRTS — Art Bible\n\n## Visual Goal\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS should present a polished, atmospheric survival world with a\ndeliberate visual language. The final bunker must not look like plain cubes,\ndefault Roblox presentation, or an arbitrary collection of props.\n\n## Bunker Mood\n\nThe starting bunker is abandoned but functional. It should feel creepy,\nindustrial, aged, and believable without losing navigational clarity.\n\nThe starting bedroom should eventually communicate this through elements such\nas:\n\n- an aged bed\n- locker or storage\n- shelving\n- believable bunker architecture\n- pipes and cables\n- industrial details\n- cobwebs\n- grime and wear\n- a flickering fluorescent fixture\n- emergency or utility lighting\n- a later usable torch/flashlight\n- a strong visual route toward the bunker interior\n\nThese are desired art-pass elements, not authorization to add them during a\nlayout or composition task.\n\n## Environment Construction Direction\n\nFuture art passes should pursue:\n\n- believable structural thickness\n- layered materials\n- trim and transitions between surfaces\n- beams and supports\n- pipes\n- cables and conduits\n- vents\n- industrial fixtures\n- purposeful clutter\n- wear, grime, and age\n- environmental storytelling\n- controlled lighting\n- strong silhouettes\n- deliberate color palette\n- high-quality composition\n\nArchitecture should read as constructed space, not thin planes or hollow cubes.\nDetail should reinforce purpose, history, scale, and navigation.\n\n## Composition Principles\n\n- Give every major space a clear purpose and focal hierarchy.\n- Use corridors, thresholds, lighting, and silhouettes to guide the player.\n- Balance enclosed tension with readable circulation.\n- Keep important routes legible even when the environment becomes detailed.\n- Compose props as part of the room's function and history, not as scattered\n  decoration.\n- Use repetition and a controlled material/color family to make the bunker\n  cohesive.\n\n## Existing Art Status\n\nThe current bunker is functional reference, not final art. Its pavement shell,\nasset geometry, materials, colors, and placement must not dictate the rebuild.\n\nThe previous `BedroomBlockout` is visually rejected. Its design and composition\nare not approved.\n\n## Phase Discipline\n\n### Design/Composition Phase\n\nAllowed:\n\n- spatial planning\n- room relationships\n- circulation\n- world placement\n- scale and silhouette studies\n- neutral blockout categories\n\nNot allowed:\n\n- final textures\n- decals\n- cobwebs\n- detailed clutter\n- final materials\n- final lighting\n- VFX\n- art polish\n\n### Art Pass\n\nAn art pass begins only after the director approves the layout and composition.\nArt direction does not authorize gameplay implementation.\n==WORLD_BIBLE==\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Task 1: additive overworld visual foundation only.\n\nPresentation geometry deliberately reserves distinct spatial opportunities for\nfuture resource gathering, scavenging, combat sightlines and exploration.  It\ncontains no gameplay IDs, prompts, scripts, remotes or reward state.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nOUTPUT = ROOT / \"src/Workspace/WorldVisualFoundation.model.json\"\nGROUND_Y = 53.4\n\nEARTH = [0.235, 0.225, 0.19]\nEARTH_DARK = [0.17, 0.17, 0.15]\nROCK = [0.29, 0.30, 0.29]\nROCK_DARK = [0.20, 0.215, 0.21]\nROCK_MOSS = [0.255, 0.285, 0.235]\nDEAD_GRASS = [0.285, 0.31, 0.22]\nWOOD = [0.255, 0.19, 0.125]\nRUST = [0.29, 0.16, 0.09]\n\n\ndef model(name, children):\n    return {\"Name\": name, \"ClassName\": \"Model\", \"Children\": children}\n\n\ndef part(name, size, pos, material, color, *, collide=False, rot=None, transparency=0.0):\n    props = {\n        \"Size\": list(size), \"Anchored\": True,\n        \"CanCollide\": collide, \"CanTouch\": False, \"CanQuery\": False,\n        \"Material\": material, \"Color\": color,\n        \"Transparency\": transparency, \"CastShadow\": True,\n    }\n    if rot is None:\n        props[\"Position\"] = list(pos)\n    else:\n        # Only Y rotations are required by this packet.\n        import math\n        a = math.radians(rot)\n        c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)\n        props[\"CFrame\"] = [pos[0], pos[1], pos[2], c, 0, s, 0, 1, 0, -s, 0, c]\n    return {\"Name\": name, \"ClassName\": \"Part\", \"Properties\": props}\n\n\ndef rock_cluster(name, x, z, scale=1.0, heading=0):\n    # Scenic, non-resource rock language. No ResourceNodeId/definition attributes.\n    return model(name, [\n        part(\"OutcropCore\", (8*scale, 3.4*scale, 6*scale), (x, GROUND_Y+1.0*scale, z), \"Slate\", ROCK, rot=heading),\n        part(\"OutcropShoulderA\", (5.2*scale, 2.5*scale, 4.5*scale), (x-4.1*scale, GROUND_Y+0.7*scale, z+1.8*scale), \"Rock\", ROCK_DARK, rot=heading+24),\n        part(\"OutcropShoulderB\", (4.5*scale, 2.1*scale, 5.0*scale), (x+4.0*scale, GROUND_Y+0.55*scale, z-1.5*scale), \"Rock\", ROCK_MOSS, rot=heading-18),\n    ])\n\n\ndef route_marker(name, x, z, heading=0):\n    # Environmental landmark, not an interaction marker.\n    return model(name, [\n        part(\"BrokenPost\", (0.65, 4.2, 0.65), (x, GROUND_Y+2.1, z), \"Wood\", WOOD, rot=heading),\n        part(\"BentCrossbar\", (4.2, 0.42, 0.5), (x+0.6, GROUND_Y+3.7, z), \"CorrodedMetal\", RUST, rot=heading+8),\n        part(\"FootingStone\", (2.8, 0.7, 2.2), (x, GROUND_Y+0.25, z), \"Rock\", ROCK_DARK, rot=heading-11),\n    ])\n\n\ndef ground_patch(name, x, z, sx, sz, heading=0):\n    return part(name, (sx, 0.18, sz), (x, GROUND_Y+0.08, z), \"Ground\", EARTH, rot=heading)\n\n\ndef build():\n    children = []\n\n    # ITERATION 4: authored bunker/farm world envelope. Scenic only; no resource IDs, prompts or gameplay state.\n    children.append(model(\"BunkerFarmWorldArtEnvelope\", [\n        # Broad overlapping ground masses remove the immediate bright-green plane reading.\n        part(\"BunkerApproachEarth\", (112, 0.30, 72), (28, GROUND_Y+0.16, 54), \"Ground\", EARTH_DARK, rot=-4),\n        part(\"FarmOuterEarth\", (74, 0.32, 66), (67, GROUND_Y+0.18, 211), \"Ground\", [0.19,0.175,0.135], rot=3),\n        part(\"FarmDisturbedSoil\", (48, 0.18, 35), (66, GROUND_Y+0.29, 214), \"Ground\", [0.145,0.13,0.095], rot=-2),\n        part(\"ServiceYardGravel\", (30, 0.20, 38), (85, GROUND_Y+0.28, 211), \"Pebble\", [0.24,0.245,0.225], rot=5),\n        part(\"BunkerFarmRoute\", (13, 0.24, 105), (53, GROUND_Y+0.30, 151), \"Ground\", [0.16,0.145,0.11], rot=-7),\n        part(\"RouteGravelSpine\", (5.5, 0.10, 94), (54, GROUND_Y+0.43, 151), \"Pebble\", [0.27,0.27,0.24], rot=-7),\n        # Safe scenic elevation at the perimeter, leaving the central farm/navigation field open.\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmWestBermA\", 38, 202, 0.82, 12),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmWestBermB\", 35, 225, 0.65, -18),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmNorthOutcrop\", 70, 244, 0.88, 8),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmEastOutcrop\", 102, 225, 0.72, -24),\n        rock_cluster(\"BunkerApproachOutcrop\", 39, 111, 0.68, 17),\n        # Foundation burial and drainage language visually seats the bunker in the earth.\n        part(\"FoundationEarthWest\", (18, 2.2, 34), (-5, GROUND_Y+0.65, 65), \"Ground\", EARTH_DARK, rot=-5),\n        part(\"FoundationEarthEast\", (18, 1.8, 40), (47, GROUND_Y+0.50, 78), \"Ground\", EARTH, rot=6),\n        part(\"FoundationRockToeA\", (15, 1.1, 5), (2, GROUND_Y+0.45, 28), \"Slate\", ROCK_DARK, rot=9),\n        part(\"FoundationRockToeB\", (13, 0.9, 5), (44, GROUND_Y+0.38, 99), \"Rock\", ROCK, rot=-11),\n        # Disturbed ground and runoff follow movement/service logic rather than decorative patches.\n        part(\"FarmWheelRutsA\", (0.65,0.06,31), (88,GROUND_Y+0.48,211), \"Ground\", [0.10,0.095,0.075], rot=4),\n        part(\"FarmWheelRutsB\", (0.65,0.06,31), (91,GROUND_Y+0.48,211), \"Ground\", [0.10,0.095,0.075], rot=4),\n        part(\"RunoffChannel\", (1.4,0.10,43), (45,GROUND_Y+0.44,207), \"Pebble\", ROCK_DARK, rot=-5),\n        # Clustered decayed vegetation: grouped edge masses, not evenly spaced trees.\n        model(\"WestDeadGrowthCluster\", [\n            part(\"DeadBrushA\", (7,0.35,5), (42,GROUND_Y+0.30,191), \"Grass\", DEAD_GRASS, rot=18),\n","metadata":{"output":"# THE OUTSKIRTS — Art Bible\n\n## Visual Goal\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS should present a polished, atmospheric survival world with a\ndeliberate visual language. The final bunker must not look like plain cubes,\ndefault Roblox presentation, or an arbitrary collection of props.\n\n## Bunker Mood\n\nThe starting bunker is abandoned but functional. It should feel creepy,\nindustrial, aged, and believable without losing navigational clarity.\n\nThe starting bedroom should eventually communicate this through elements such\nas:\n\n- an aged bed\n- locker or storage\n- shelving\n- believable bunker architecture\n- pipes and cables\n- industrial details\n- cobwebs\n- grime and wear\n- a flickering fluorescent fixture\n- emergency or utility lighting\n- a later usable torch/flashlight\n- a strong visual route toward the bunker interior\n\nThese are desired art-pass elements, not authorization to add them during a\nlayout or composition task.\n\n## Environment Construction Direction\n\nFuture art passes should pursue:\n\n- believable structural thickness\n- layered materials\n- trim and transitions between surfaces\n- beams and supports\n- pipes\n- cables and conduits\n- vents\n- industrial fixtures\n- purposeful clutter\n- wear, grime, and age\n- environmental storytelling\n- controlled lighting\n- strong silhouettes\n- deliberate color palette\n- high-quality composition\n\nArchitecture should read as constructed space, not thin planes or hollow cubes.\nDetail should reinforce purpose, history, scale, and navigation.\n\n## Composition Principles\n\n- Give every major space a clear purpose and focal hierarchy.\n- Use corridors, thresholds, lighting, and silhouettes to guide the player.\n- Balance enclosed tension with readable circulation.\n- Keep important routes legible even when the environment becomes detailed.\n- Compose props as part of the room's function and history, not as scattered\n  decoration.\n- Use repetition and a controlled material/color family to make the bunker\n  cohesive.\n\n## Existing Art Status\n\nThe current bunker is functional reference, not final art. Its pavement shell,\nasset geometry, materials, colors, and placement must not dictate the rebuild.\n\nThe previous `BedroomBlockout` is visually rejected. Its design and composition\nare not approved.\n\n## Phase Discipline\n\n### Design/Composition Phase\n\nAllowed:\n\n- spatial planning\n- room relationships\n- circulation\n- world placement\n- scale and silhouette studies\n- neutral blockout categories\n\nNot allowed:\n\n- final textures\n- decals\n- cobwebs\n- detailed clutter\n- final materials\n- final lighting\n- VFX\n- art polish\n\n### Art Pass\n\nAn art pass begins only after the director approves the layout and composition.\nArt direction does not authorize gameplay implementation.\n==WORLD_BIBLE==\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Task 1: additive overworld visual foundation only.\n\nPresentation geometry deliberately reserves distinct spatial opportunities for\nfuture resource gathering, scavenging, combat sightlines and exploration.  It\ncontains no gameplay IDs, prompts, scripts, remotes or reward state.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nOUTPUT = ROOT / \"src/Workspace/WorldVisualFoundation.model.json\"\nGROUND_Y = 53.4\n\nEARTH = [0.235, 0.225, 0.19]\nEARTH_DARK = [0.17, 0.17, 0.15]\nROCK = [0.29, 0.30, 0.29]\nROCK_DARK = [0.20, 0.215, 0.21]\nROCK_MOSS = [0.255, 0.285, 0.235]\nDEAD_GRASS = [0.285, 0.31, 0.22]\nWOOD = [0.255, 0.19, 0.125]\nRUST = [0.29, 0.16, 0.09]\n\n\ndef model(name, children):\n    return {\"Name\": name, \"ClassName\": \"Model\", \"Children\": children}\n\n\ndef part(name, size, pos, material, color, *, collide=False, rot=None, transparency=0.0):\n    props = {\n        \"Size\": list(size), \"Anchored\": True,\n        \"CanCollide\": collide, \"CanTouch\": False, \"CanQuery\": False,\n        \"Material\": material, \"Color\": color,\n        \"Transparency\": transparency, \"CastShadow\": True,\n    }\n    if rot is None:\n        props[\"Position\"] = list(pos)\n    else:\n        # Only Y rotations are required by this packet.\n        import math\n        a = math.radians(rot)\n        c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)\n        props[\"CFrame\"] = [pos[0], pos[1], pos[2], c, 0, s, 0, 1, 0, -s, 0, c]\n    return {\"Name\": name, \"ClassName\": \"Part\", \"Properties\": props}\n\n\ndef rock_cluster(name, x, z, scale=1.0, heading=0):\n    # Scenic, non-resource rock language. No ResourceNodeId/definition attributes.\n    return model(name, [\n        part(\"OutcropCore\", (8*scale, 3.4*scale, 6*scale), (x, GROUND_Y+1.0*scale, z), \"Slate\", ROCK, rot=heading),\n        part(\"OutcropShoulderA\", (5.2*scale, 2.5*scale, 4.5*scale), (x-4.1*scale, GROUND_Y+0.7*scale, z+1.8*scale), \"Rock\", ROCK_DARK, rot=heading+24),\n        part(\"OutcropShoulderB\", (4.5*scale, 2.1*scale, 5.0*scale), (x+4.0*scale, GROUND_Y+0.55*scale, z-1.5*scale), \"Rock\", ROCK_MOSS, rot=heading-18),\n    ])\n\n\ndef route_marker(name, x, z, heading=0):\n    # Environmental landmark, not an interaction marker.\n    return model(name, [\n        part(\"BrokenPost\", (0.65, 4.2, 0.65), (x, GROUND_Y+2.1, z), \"Wood\", WOOD, rot=heading),\n        part(\"BentCrossbar\", (4.2, 0.42, 0.5), (x+0.6, GROUND_Y+3.7, z), \"CorrodedMetal\", RUST, rot=heading+8),\n        part(\"FootingStone\", (2.8, 0.7, 2.2), (x, GROUND_Y+0.25, z), \"Rock\", ROCK_DARK, rot=heading-11),\n    ])\n\n\ndef ground_patch(name, x, z, sx, sz, heading=0):\n    return part(name, (sx, 0.18, sz), (x, GROUND_Y+0.08, z), \"Ground\", EARTH, rot=heading)\n\n\ndef build():\n    children = []\n\n    # ITERATION 4: authored bunker/farm world envelope. Scenic only; no resource IDs, prompts or gameplay state.\n    children.append(model(\"BunkerFarmWorldArtEnvelope\", [\n        # Broad overlapping ground masses remove the immediate bright-green plane reading.\n        part(\"BunkerApproachEarth\", (112, 0.30, 72), (28, GROUND_Y+0.16, 54), \"Ground\", EARTH_DARK, rot=-4),\n        part(\"FarmOuterEarth\", (74, 0.32, 66), (67, GROUND_Y+0.18, 211), \"Ground\", [0.19,0.175,0.135], rot=3),\n        part(\"FarmDisturbedSoil\", (48, 0.18, 35), (66, GROUND_Y+0.29, 214), \"Ground\", [0.145,0.13,0.095], rot=-2),\n        part(\"ServiceYardGravel\", (30, 0.20, 38), (85, GROUND_Y+0.28, 211), \"Pebble\", [0.24,0.245,0.225], rot=5),\n        part(\"BunkerFarmRoute\", (13, 0.24, 105), (53, GROUND_Y+0.30, 151), \"Ground\", [0.16,0.145,0.11], rot=-7),\n        part(\"RouteGravelSpine\", (5.5, 0.10, 94), (54, GROUND_Y+0.43, 151), \"Pebble\", [0.27,0.27,0.24], rot=-7),\n        # Safe scenic elevation at the perimeter, leaving the central farm/navigation field open.\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmWestBermA\", 38, 202, 0.82, 12),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmWestBermB\", 35, 225, 0.65, -18),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmNorthOutcrop\", 70, 244, 0.88, 8),\n        rock_cluster(\"FarmEastOutcrop\", 102, 225, 0.72, -24),\n        rock_cluster(\"BunkerApproachOutcrop\", 39, 111, 0.68, 17),\n        # Foundation burial and drainage language visually seats the bunker in the earth.\n        part(\"FoundationEarthWest\", (18, 2.2, 34), (-5, GROUND_Y+0.65, 65), \"Ground\", EARTH_DARK, rot=-5),\n        part(\"FoundationEarthEast\", (18, 1.8, 40), (47, GROUND_Y+0.50, 78), \"Ground\", EARTH, rot=6),\n        part(\"FoundationRockToeA\", (15, 1.1, 5), (2, GROUND_Y+0.45, 28), \"Slate\", ROCK_DARK, rot=9),\n        part(\"FoundationRockToeB\", (13, 0.9, 5), (44, GROUND_Y+0.38, 99), \"Rock\", ROCK, rot=-11),\n        # Disturbed ground and runoff follow movement/service logic rather than decorative patches.\n        part(\"FarmWheelRutsA\", (0.65,0.06,31), (88,GROUND_Y+0.48,211), \"Ground\", [0.10,0.095,0.075], rot=4),\n        part(\"FarmWheelRutsB\", (0.65,0.06,31), (91,GROUND_Y+0.48,211), \"Ground\", [0.10,0.095,0.075], rot=4),\n        part(\"RunoffChannel\", (1.4,0.10,43), (45,GROUND_Y+0.44,207), \"Pebble\", ROCK_DARK, rot=-5),\n        # Clustered decayed vegetation: grouped edge masses, not evenly spaced trees.\n        model(\"WestDeadGrowthCluster\", [\n            part(\"DeadBrushA\", (7,0.35,5), (42,GROUND_Y+0.30,191), \"Grass\", DEAD_GRASS, rot=18),\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat docs/director/ART-BIBLE.md 2>&1; echo \"==WORLD_BIBLE==\"; cat tools/builders/generate_world_visual_foundation.py 2>&1 | head -n 100","time":{"start":1788174376551,"end":1788174376554}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a0577f9c2e7ca18dd0427ec2364f59"}},"id":"prt_0577f9e2b00117dJitusuLfG7X","sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","messageID":"msg_0577f958f001einhVsrNVYksP5"}}
