{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788175183722,"sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a057800fd9742381106a2d53c41eca","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Qwen world reasoning","prompt":"You are QWEN master-reasoner for BunkerGame. Analyze the requirement to create a genuinely NEW large survival world.\n\nContext:\n- Old rejected world is in ServerStorage.NOT IN USE.GameWorld - archive only, DO NOT reuse.\n- Workspace currently appears empty in Studio (only Terrain/Camera/Runtime), but filesystem still has src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json (canonical flat world with frozen coordinates) and SyntheticSolApproach/CollapsedServiceApproach models now archived.\n- Canonical contracts in docs/director/FULL-GAME-CONTRACTS.md define frozen gameplay: 6 spawns at bedroom, 18 trees, 6 scrap caches, 7 zombie spawns, 12 plots, processor, stations, datum Y=54, bounds -320..320, -240..400.\n- Visual reference is the approved Art Bible / Environment Art Bible / SOL_GATE1 golden reference at artifacts/sol-gate1-golden-reference - which shows terrain-driven dogleg, delayed visibility, buried facility, heavy asymmetry, terrain dominance.\n- Must create new world that feels LARGE, creepy, forest with density gradients, convincing terrain (rolling, ridges, valleys, not flat slabs), ground dressing clusters, rocks/boulders as terrain language, landmarks, bunker embedded into landscape, wildlife, atmosphere with depth, gameplay integration, performance budgets.\n- Asset library currently has: bunker_electrical_junction_box_01, bunker_valve_assembly_01, bunker_vent_grille_01, old_military_ammo_crate_01, pipeline_pipe_retry_02 (registry-only), natural_boulder_sandstone_01.\n\nTask:\n1. Extract reference language from SOL golden reference and Art Bible: terrain language, vegetation density/silhouette/spacing, elevation, path, rock distribution, landmark hierarchy, atmospheric depth, lighting, palette, layering, scale, negative space, horror mood.\n2. Reason about world topology that satisfies both \"LARGE survival landscape\" and frozen contracts. Propose zones: bunker + entrance yard + starter forest + east forest + farm + salvage route + zombie arc, but reimagined with terrain variation, forest gradients, landmarks. Address how to preserve frozen tree/scrap/zombie positions while making world feel natural (adjust dressing, add terrain around them, density gradients near them).\n3. Provide composition planning: focal hierarchy, sightlines, controlled breaks, landmarks that aid navigation, bunker embedment strategy, terrain occlusion.\n4. Provide generation strategy: what should be Terrain vs parts, what asset families needed, what reusable assets to extend, what new native generation needed (trees, rocks, boulders, landmarks).\n5. Output provenance classification QWEN_REFERENCE_SOURCE.\n\nBe concise but thorough. Output structured reasoning with measurable constraints where possible. This is reasoning only, no implementation.","subagent_type":"bunkergame-master-reasoner"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_fa87fdbecffeQMDJxZ4rwat427\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nUnderstood. The **bunkergame-native-asset-pipeline** skill is loaded.\n\nI am ready to generate reasoning packets for visual asset requests following this production chain:\n\n**`User → Muse → Qwen (Qwen) → Muse → MiMo → Roblox Assistant ↔ BloxForge → Muse Final Review → Asset Library → Rojo → Studio Verification`**\n\n---\n\n### What I Do For Each Request\n\nWhen you provide a request such as:\n- *\"תעשה עצים אמיתיים\"* (make real trees)\n- *\"תפזר אבנים ברחבי המפה\"* (scatter rocks across the map)\n- *\"תעשה וריאציה של העץ הזה לביום אחר\"* (make a variation of this tree for another biome)\n\nI will output:\n\n| Category | Content |\n|----------|---------|\n| **Actual Objective** | What must technically happen |\n| **Player-Facing Objective** | What the player experiences |\n| **Constraints** | Hard requirements, limits |\n| **Dependencies** | Assets/tools/info needed first |\n| **Contradictions** | Conflicting requirements |\n| **Risks** | Potential failure modes |\n| **Decisions Required** | Choices waiting on Muse/user |\n| **Recommended Reasoning Strategy** | How Qwen should approach this |\n\nPlus the required **provenance classification**:\n\n```\nQWEN_REFERENCE_SOURCE=USER_REFERENCE|LIBRARY_REFERENCE|QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE|ONLINE_REFERENCE|NONE\n```\n\n---\n\n### I Will NOT:\n- Perform Art Director approval (that's Muse's role)\n- Implement assets directly (that's MiMo/Assistant/BloxForge's role)\n- Fabricate participation evidence\n- Revive old tasks from conversation history\n\n---\n\n**REASONING_PACKET_READY=YES**\n\nPlease provide your asset request.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","sessionId":"ses_fa87fdbecffeQMDJxZ4rwat427","model":{"providerID":"ollama","modelID":"qwen-spatial"},"truncated":false},"title":"Qwen world reasoning","time":{"start":1788174410777,"end":1788175183708}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a057800fd9742381106a2d53c41eca"}},"id":"prt_057800f92001JBDJ4EOGgjhpBN","sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","messageID":"msg_0577fec4d001H47LyR3p28sd5k"}}
