{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788178143202,"sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a057a151e67b528ff6a2c6c0ba9d5c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Spatial plan for large world","prompt":"You are bunkergame-spatial-architect. Convert BunkerGame new world creative intent into measurable implementation-ready spatial specification.\n\nCREATIVE INTENT:\n- LARGE creepy survival landscape, forest, rolling terrain, ridges/valleys, forest density gradients, rock formation language, landmarks for navigation/storytelling, bunker built INTO hillside not on top, atmospheric depth, survival horror mood, believable scale.\n- Must preserve frozen gameplay anchors: bunker bounds X -62..58 Z 14..158, 6 bedroom spawns, 18 trees at fixed positions (west/east forests), 6 scrap caches south, 7 zombie spawns southern arc >200 studs from spawns, 12 plots at 75,85,95,105 x 200,210,220, processor at 121,210, plus 7 stations inside bunker. World datum Y=54, StableGround 640x640 central.\n- Reference language from SOL golden: one coherent landform, terrain-driven dogleg, delayed visibility, reveal beat, buried facility, direct terrain contact, player-scale traversal (10 stud clear primary paths, 8 secondary, 7 doors, 9 headroom), asymmetry, depth layers, terrain dominance 70/30.\n- Must avoid: flat slabs, repetitive wedges, evenly spaced grid forest, identical tree rotation/scale, flat world, isolated bunker box, straight approach revealing facade early.\n\nREQUIRED SPATIAL CONTRACT:\n1. PLAYER EXPERIENCE: emotional sequence wake -> commons -> entrance yard -> exterior Curiosity -> forest traversal -> landmarks -> farm -> salvage route threat lanes.\n2. ROUTE INTENT: start bedroom exit south to entrance at (0,54,20), then to farm gate (52,155), then to fields. Require lateral movement, direction changes, forbidden shortcuts.\n3. VISIBILITY CONTRACT: checkpoints P0-P4 with target ranges for visibility.\n4. MASSING CONTRACT: dominant terrain mass, secondary masses, hierarchy, overburden, recess, silhouette.\n5. OCCLUSION CONTRACT: what blocks what at which checkpoint.\n6. NEGATIVE SPACE: protected traversal volumes, reveal corridors.\n7. VISUAL LANGUAGE: material hierarchy, vegetation hierarchy, lighting intent.\n8. HARD ANTI-GOALS: list forbidden outcomes.\n\nAlso specify:\n- Route checkpoints coordinates, terrain mass centers/dimensions/elevations, occlusion relationships, negative volumes, silhouette hierarchy, builder MUST/MUST NOT.\n\nEnd with SPATIAL_SPEC_READY=YES if complete. Do not invent final coordinates for bunker interior; keep existing bunker but embed it.\n\nWorkspace placement: must use filesystem src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json as persistence. Currently Workspace empty. New world should be generated via tools/builders/generate_full_game_world.py modified to add terrain/forest dressing while preserving gameplay IDs, plus new dressing models.\n\nProvide spec.","subagent_type":"bunkergame-spatial-architect"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_fa85e9058ffeMIQPNkzdCZhZfD\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# BUNKERGAME SPATIAL SPECIFICATION\n\n## CONTEXT & CONSTRAINTS VERIFICATION\n\n**Frozen Gameplay Anchors (PRESERVE EXACT):**\n| Anchor | Type | Coordinates/Bounds |\n|--------|------|-------------------|\n| World Datum | Y-reference | Y=54 |\n| StableGround | Central plateau | 640×640 studs centered |\n| Bunker Bounds | XZ bounds | X: -62..58, Z: 14..158 |\n| Bunker Elevation | Vertical range | Embedded into hillside (see below) |\n| Bedroom Spawns | Count | 6 |\n| Entrance Point | Route checkpoint | (0, 54, 20) |\n| Farm Gate | Route checkpoint | (52, 155) |\n| Trees | Fixed positions | 18 total (west/east forests - preserve existing) |\n| Scrap Caches | Count/zone | 6, south of bunker |\n| Zombie Spawns | Count/zone/radius | 7, southern arc, >200 studs from spawns |\n| Farm Plots | Grid | 12 plots at X={75,85,95,105} × Z={200,210,220} |\n| Processor | Fixed location | (121, 210) |\n\n**Style Contract (SOL Golden):**\n- One coherent landform ✓\n- Terrain-driven dogleg ✓\n- Delayed visibility ✓\n- Reveal beat ✓\n- Buried facility ✓\n- Direct terrain contact ✓\n- Asymmetry ✓\n- Depth layers ✓\n- Terrain dominance 70/30 ✓\n\n---\n\n## SPATIAL SPECIFICATION\n\n### 1. PLAYER EXPERIENCE SEQUENCE\n\n| Phase | Location | Emotional Intent | Spatial Characteristic |\n|-------|----------|------------------|----------------------|\n| **P0: WAKE** | Bedroom spawn → Interior Commons | Disorientation → Mild Safety | Enclosed, bounded Y-height (~9 studs headroom), limited sightline to exterior |\n| **P1: EXIT** | Entrance Yard | Curiosity + Exposure Threshold | Transition from interior → semi-enclosed yard (10-20 stud lateral clear) |\n| **P2: REVEAL** | Exterior Approach (Z~30..50) | First Landmark Recognition, Scale Realization | Delayed full bunker visibility; terraced reveal of massing only |\n| **P3: TRAVERSAL** | Forest Edge → Ridge Line | Uncertainty + Navigation Challenge | Vertical displacement required; lateral movement 10-30 studs; sightline to farm |\n| **P4: ARRIVAL** | Farm Entry Point (52, 155) | Relief + Purpose | Opening into cultivated negative space; fields visible beyond |\n\n---\n\n### 2. ROUTE & CHECKPOINT CONTRACT\n\n#### Primary Route Geometry:\n```\nROUTE: P0 → P1 → P2 → P3 → P4\n        ↓     ↓     ↓     ↓     ↓\n   BEDROOM ENTRANCE TERRACE RIDGE   FARM_GATE\n         (X=0,Z=20)   (Z~40)  (Z~70-90)   (X=52,Z=155)\n```\n\n#### Checkpoint Coordinates & Dimensions:\n\n| CP | X Range | Z Range | Y Elevation Range | Terrain Relationship |\n|----|---------|---------|------------------|---------------------|\n| **P0** | -10..10 | 30..62* | 54..63 (interior) | Interior, below grade contact only |\n| **P1** | -20..20 | 0..20 | 54..58 | Bunker entrance yard; partially sheltered |\n| **P2** | -30..80 | 25..55 | 56..72 (rising) | Exterior terrace; begins ridge approach |\n| **P3** | -40..100 | 60..95 | 58..78 (peak ~75-85) | Ridge crest; forced lateral displacement |\n| **P4** | 40..70 | 145..160 | 54..62 (descending) | Farm approach; negative-space opening |\n\n*Note: Bunker extends to Z=158, but P0 interior stays within bounds\n\n#### Route Constraints:\n- **Lateral Displacement Required:** Minimum 3 direction changes from P0→P4\n- **Vertical Displacement:** Cumulative elevation change ≥25 studs (ridge climb)\n- **Forbidden Shortcuts:** No direct straight-line path from bunker entrance to farm without crossing terrain crest\n- **Primary Path Width:** 10 stud clear minimum\n- **Secondary Path Width:** 8 stud clear minimum\n- **Player Headroom:** 9 studs minimum at all route checkpoints\n\n#### Approach Vector Angles (from Bunker):\n| Segment | Lateral Angle (°) | Vertical Grade (%) | Intent |\n|---------|------------------|--------------------|---------|\n| P1→P2 | 0..30° right | +5-12% | Gradual ascent, delayed horizon reveal |\n| P2→P3 | 15..45° left | +8-20% | Ridge climb (dogleg turn) |\n| P3→P4 | 0..20° right | -10..-25% | Descent into farm valley |\n\n---\n\n### 3. VISIBILITY CONTRACT\n\n| Checkpoint | Bunker Visibility % | Landmark(s) Visible | Farm Visibility % | Forest Density Zone |\n|------------|-------------------|---------------------|------------------|--------------------|\n| **P0** (Bedroom) | 0-5% (interior only) | None | 0% | 0% |\n| **P1** (Entrance Yard) | 10-25% (partial facade) | Ridge crest silhouette only | 0% | Low (20-30%) |\n| **P2** (Terrace) | 35-55% (embedded massing visible) | Ridge crest + distant farm treeline | 5-15% (glimpse) | Medium (40-50%) |\n| **P3** (Ridge Crest) | 60-85% (majority of bunker in view) | Full farm fields, processor | 70-90% | High (60-80%, framing shot) |\n| **P4** (Farm Gate) | 25-40% (bunker recedes/occluded by ridges) | None (player is now at destination) | 100% (immediate) | Medium-High edge zone |\n\n#### Visibility Thresholds:\n- **Bunker Full Reveal:** NOT until P3 (ridge crest only)\n- **Farm First Glimpse:** At P2, max 15% visible (through tree gap)\n- **Reveal Beat Timing:** Farm first fully visible at P3 after climbing the ridge\n\n---\n\n### 4. MASSING CONTRACT\n\n#### Primary Terrain Mass:\n```\nDOMINANT TERRAIN: Ridge Line + Hillside Embedding\n\nCenter of Mass: ~(-20, 68, 50) [X, Y-elev avg, Z]\nPrimary Extent: X -120..100, Z 30..180\nPeak Elevation: Y 78-88 (ridge crest behind bunker)\nBunker Embed Depth: Bunker facade ~60% below ridge crests\n\nTERRAIN/BUCKNER SILHOUETTE RATIO: 70:30 (minimum when viewed from P3)\n```\n\n#### Secondary Masses:\n\n| Mass ID | X Range | Z Range | Y Elev. Range | Relationship to Bunker |\n|---------|---------|---------|--------------|------------------------|\n| **H1** (Main Ridge Behind) | -80..40 | 25..60 | 72-90 | Overburden mass; occludes bunker from north |\n| **H2** (Left Shoulder) | -120..-30 | 50..130 | 68-85 | Frames left side of traverse route |\n| **H3** (Right Drop-off) | 80..180 | 90..220 | 54-66 | Creates right-side negative space toward farm |\n| **H4** (Forest Ridge East) | 100..220 | 140..180 | 60-75 | Border mass for farm zone |\n\n#### Mass Hierarchy:\n```\nTier 1 (Dominant): H1 Main Ridge - occupies 35-45% of vertical silhouette from P3\nTier 2 (Secondary): H2, H4 - occupy 20-30% combined\nTier 3 (Tertiary): Bunker facade visible - max 30% when at P2-P3\n```\n\n#### Embedment Requirements:\n- **Bunker Rear Contact:** Direct terrain contact along full rear wall at Z~158, Y=54..68\n- **Side Contact:** Left flank (X=-62) must have terrain within 15 studs for 70% of bunker height\n- **Facade Exposure:** Right face (toward farm) has max 25% exposed from Z<130 view angle\n- **Overburden Volume:** Terrain volume above bunker roof ≥80% of bunker internal volume\n\n---\n\n### 5. OCCLUSION CONTRACT\n\n| Checkpoint | What Is Occluded | By Which Mass | Occlusion % at CP |\n|------------|----------------|---------------|------------------|\n| **P1** → North/South | Farm, Processor, South scrap caches | H1 ridge + bunker own mass | 85-95% |\n| **P2** → East | Full farm access, zombie arc | H2 left shoulder + tree screen | 70-80% |\n| **P3** → Back (bunker rear) | Bunker interior/entrance | Player elevation advantage + own ridge | Self-occluded; player sees 85% from crest |\n| **P4** → North/West | Bunker full approach, bedroom spawns | H1 rear ridge + H2 left mass | 60-75% |\n\n#### Occlusion Volumes Defined:\n```\nVOC-01 (Bunker Shelter):\nBounds: X -30..30, Z 0..40, Y 54..70\nFunction: Keeps player \"inside\" terrain until P2 threshold\n\nVOC-02 (Forest Screen):\nBounds: X -100..50, Z 60..180, Y 54..75+\nFunction: Dense vegetation occludes direct line-of-sight to farm until P3\n\nVOC-03 (Ridge Overhang):\nBounds: X -20..60, Z 20..50, Y 70..90 (peak)\nFunction: Main occlusion of bunker from southern approach views\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. NEGATIVE SPACE VOLUMES\n\n| Negative ID | Function | Boundaries | Dimensions |\n|-------------|----------|------------|------------|\n| **NS-01** | Entrance Yard Buffer | Bunker entrance + terrace | 30×40 studs at P1, Y=54..62 |\n| **NS-02** | Ridge Traverse Corridor | Along ridge crest path | 15 stud wide minimum along Z=50..90 |\n| **NS-03** | Farm Approach Opening | Between H3 right drop + farm treeline | 40×60 studs, opens at P4 |\n| **NS-04** | Threat Lane (Salvage Route) | Parallel to primary route; offset left | Secondary 8-stud path between tree gaps |\n\n#### Protected Volumes:\n```\nTRAVEL-P1 (Primary Path Through Forest):\nStarts: Z=55 near terrace exit\nEnds: Z=92 at ridge crest entry\nWidth: 10 studs (min), 14 studs (nominal)\nHeight Clearance: 9 studs min to tree canopy/geometry\n\nTRAVEL-P4 (Farm Entry Negative Space):\nStarts: P3→P4 descent terminus\nEnds: Farm gate at (52, 155)\nWidth: 25-35 studs opening into farm\nVisual Intent: Contrasts with dense forest via sudden negative space\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. VISUAL LANGUAGE (MEASURABLE HIERARCHY)\n\n#### Material Layering:\n\n| Layer | Coverage Ratio | Placement Rule |\n|-------|---------------|----------------|\n| **T1** (Exposed rock/slate) | 5-8% of terrain surface | Ridge crests, erosion lines where Y>70 |\n| **T2** (Dirt/gravel transitions) | 15-20% | Path edges, slope transitions (grade >15%) |\n| **T3** (Loam/organic) | 40-50% | Primary ground plane at Y=54..60 |\n| **T4** (Dense vegetation coverage) | 25-35% | Forest zones, especially between P2-P3 |\n\n#### Vegetation Hierarchy:\n\n```\nZONE A (Bunker Immediate): Trees ≤10 mature specimens, spacing ≥8 studs apart\n  Rationale: Maintain bunker presence + sightlines\n\nZONE B (Terrace Transition): Mixed density 40-50%, trees at 12-20 stud separation\n  Rationale: Frame P2 visibility without full occlusion\n\nZONE C (Ridge Traverse): High density 65-80%, tree spacing 8-12 studs, varied heights\n  Rationale: Challenge navigation + control sightlines\n\nZONE D (Farm Approach): Decreasing density gradient from 70% → 40% as player approaches P4\n  Rationale: Visual release upon farm arrival\n```\n\n#### Lighting Intent:\n```\nBUNKER FACADE ILLUMINATION: Partially shadowed by ridge overhang H1 when viewed from P3\nFOREST CANOPY DENSITY: Block ~65-75% of overhead in Zone C, 40-50% in Zone B\nFARM OPENING: 85-95% light exposure (contrast with forest)\nTIMING IMPACT: Evening/shorelight enhances bunker shadow depth for horror mood\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. HARD ANTI-GOALS (MUST NOT)\n\n| Forbidden Outcome | Detection Rule | Correction |\n|------------------|----------------|------------|\n| Flat world appearance | Terrain variance <15 studs within 200 stud radius of P0-P4 | Add rolling ridges, valleys ≥6-8 stud depth variation |\n| Isolated bunker box | Bunker visible >40% from Z<20 southern approach | Increase H1 overburden + add screening vegetation |\n| Straight-line shortcut to farm | Direct path exists without vertical crest crossing at P3 | Add ridge blocking with 8+ stud elevation barrier |\n| Grid-tree forest appearance | >40% tree positions align within ±5 studs on orthogonal grid | Introduce organic scatter, varied rotations (±15-45°), scale variance (0.7-1.3) |\n| Early full bunker reveal from entrance zone | Bunker >55% visible before P3 | Add terracing + vegetation screen; increase H1 height to Y=82+ minimum |\n| Repetitive wedge geometry | 3+ consecutive terrain sections with same slope angle within 10° | Vary pitch every 20-30 studs along primary route |\n\n---\n\n### 9. BUILDER REQUIREMENTS (MUST / MUST NOT)\n\n#### MUST DO:\n```\n✓ Create one coherent landform (not multiple disconnected islands)\n✓ Embed bunker into hillside with direct terrain contact on rear + left flanks\n✓ Establish dogleg route requiring 3+ direction changes from P0→P4\n✓ Maintain 70/30 terrain-to-bunker silhouette ratio at P3 viewpoint\n✓ Achieve visibility progression: 0-5% → 10-25% → 35-55% → 60-85% → 25-40% (bunker only)\n✓ Create ridge crest elevation ≥ Y78 at P3 checkpoint\n✓ Preserve all frozen gameplay anchors exactly as specified\n✓ Add forest density gradients: Low (P1) → Medium-High (P2-P3) → Edge zone (P4)\n✓ Maintain 10-stud primary path clearance throughout route\n```\n\n#### MUST NOT DO:\n```\n✗ Move or resize bunkers, plots, processor, spawn points (frozen anchors only)\n✗ Allow straight-line sightline from bunker entrance to farm without crest crossing\n✗ Create flat terrain sections >40 studs in any direction along primary route\n✗ Place trees in grid-aligned patterns; MUST use varied rotation/scale/spacing\n✗ Expose full bunker face before P3 checkpoint location\n✗ Build isolated bunker with minimal terrain contact (must be embedded)\n✗ Violate player headroom <9 studs on any route segment\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES\n\n#### File System & Persistence:\n- **Primary persistence:** `src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json`\n- **Generation tool:** `tools/builders/generate_full_game_world.py` (to be modified for terrain + forest dressing)\n- **Frozen asset IDs:** Bunker, 6 bedroom spawns, 18 trees, 6 scrap caches, 7 zombie spawns, 12 plots, processor preserve existing instance IDs\n\n#### Builder Coordination:\n- Use `rbx-create-skill` for major art build orchestration (Muse → Qwen → MiMo → Roblox Assistant)\n- Use `rbx-scene-analysis` to verify terrain complexity + memory budget post-generation\n- Verify via Studio playtest that route forces dogleg traversal (cannot shortcut to farm)\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY VERIFICATION\n\n✓ Player experience sequence defined (P0→P4 emotional arc)  \n✓ Route geometry with coordinates and constraints specified  \n✓ Visibility contract with percentages at 5 checkpoints  \n✓ Massing hierarchy with terrain dominance ratio  \n✓ Occlusion relationships mapped per checkpoint  \n✓ Negative space volumes defined for traversal  \n✓ Visual language with material/vegetation/lighting layers  \n✓ Hard anti-goals listed with detection rules  \n✓ Builder MUST/MUST NOT requirements explicit  \n✓ Frozen gameplay anchors preserved  \n\n---\n\n**SPATIAL_SPEC_READY=YES**\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","sessionId":"ses_fa85e9058ffeMIQPNkzdCZhZfD","model":{"providerID":"ollama","modelID":"qwen-spatial"},"truncated":false},"title":"Spatial plan for large world","time":{"start":1788176592812,"end":1788178143188}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a057a151e67b528ff6a2c6c0ba9d5c"}},"id":"prt_057a151ca0017mroASVgIVp0VM","sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","messageID":"msg_057a13bf2001d60DXlr7AsLHLf"}}
