{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788179421109,"sessionID":"ses_fa8815f1bffeeE6hC19uqKKiGR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a057c093e57111865b9b7a34dfaaec","state":{"status":"error","input":{"description":"Build new large world","prompt":"You are bunker-builder, implementation worker for BunkerGame. Execute concrete implementation brief for genuinely NEW large survival world.\n\nDIRECTOR BRIEF:\nGoal: Create genuinely NEW, LARGE, HIGH-QUALITY creepy survival world in src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json, that feels like a believable landscape not flat baseplate. Preserve frozen gameplay contracts but transform visual dressing.\n\nSAFETY:\n- Old rejected world is ServerStorage.NOT IN USE.GameWorld (archived). DO NOT move it back. OLD_REJECTED_WORLD_REUSED must = NO. Verify via Studio that Workspace currently EMPTY (only Terrain/Runtime) and NOT IN USE holds archives.\n- Filesystem source of truth: src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json is currently canonical flat bunker (1.1MB). You must CREATE NEW world that preserves frozen anchors but adds large terrain/forest/rocks/landmarks/atmosphere. Do not delete frozen IDs.\n- Before any destructive Rojo sync, inspect what will change, preserve recovery evidence.\n\nFROZEN CONTRACTS TO PRESERVE (exact positions, IDs, attributes):\n- Spawns 6 at (-49..-33,54.5,62/72), facing bedroom exit, SpawnId bedroom_01..06\n- Stations 8 at specific positions (power_console 34,56.5,71 etc see FULL-GAME-CONTRACTS)\n- 12 plots at X 75,85,95,105 Z 200,210,220 Y54.25, PlotId plot_01..12\n- Processor at 121,55.5,210\n- 18 trees at fixed positions list in contracts (preserved but dressed to feel forest)\n- 6 scrap caches and 7 zombie spawns southern arc\n- Foundation StableGround at (0,52.5,80) size 640x3x640, datum Y54, playable boundaries\n- Bunker architecture X -62..58 Z14..158 (keep but embed into terrain)\n- Lighting/Atmosphere budgets within limits\n\nREFERENCE LANGUAGE (from SOL golden + Art Bible):\n- Terrain: rolling elevation, ridges/valleys, berms, depressions, natural slopes, irregular silhouettes, one coherent landform, 70/30 terrain dominance\n- Vegetation: density gradients (dense/medium/sparse/clearings/disturbed), not grid, silhouette variation, multiple variants\n- Ground: clustered dressing (grasses, weeds, stones, branches, disturbed soil) not uniform scatter\n- Rocks: isolated boulders, clusters, exposed formations, slope reinforcement\n- Landmarks: 3-5 strong memorable (radio, ruins, checkpoint) not many weak props\n- Bunker: buried, partial concealment, earth contact, drainage, anticipation\n- Atmosphere: fog, color correction, depth, playable darkness\n- Palette: damp concrete, corroded steel, muted sage/brown, amber utility, sparse red\n\nSPATIAL SPEC READY: See previous spatial spec with checkpoints P0-P4, masses H1-H4, route with dogleg, visibility progression 0%->85%, negative spaces.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION TASKS:\n1. Inspect current filesystem GameWorld.model.json and Studio state. Verify Rojo 7.7.0 at $HOME/.aftman/bin/rojo, run rojo sourcemap to verify mapping.\n2. Create new world builder or directly edit GameWorld.model.json to add:\n   - Large terrain dressing: Create new Model \"TerrainDressing\" under GameWorld with rolling hills using WedgePart/Part tilted (30-35 deg) to form coherent landform around bunker and forests. Hills should embed bunker (rear contact Z158, side contact), ridge behind at Y78-88, left shoulder -120..-30, right drop, forest ridge east. Budget 80-120 parts for terrain masses. No flat slabs.\n   - Forest system: Under Resources.Trees dressing, add forest understory: For each of 18 tree positions, add 2-3 additional dressing trees/bushes with varied scale 0.7-1.3, rotation variance, to create density gradients. Use natural_boulder_sandstone_01 family and generate new tree variants via native generation if possible, otherwise use Part-based trunks with varied canopies. Dense at P3 ridge (65-80%), medium at terrace, low near bunker. Exclude grid placement.\n   - Rocks: Add RockFormations model with isolated boulders, clusters at slope reinforcements, path edges, using natural_boulder_sandstone_01 as base. Vary scale/rotation, avoid repeats.\n   - Landmarks: 3 strong: abandoned radio tower near east forest (approx 200,80), ruined checkpoint near entrance yard (-5,20), farm outbuilding ruins near farm gate (50,160). Each small but memorable, using available GeneratedAssets plus primitive dressing.\n   - Ground detail: Add GroundDressing model with clustered grasses/weeds/stones/branches using small Parts with material variation, clustered not uniform.\n   - Atmosphere: Add/verify Lighting model with fog, ColorCorrection for depth, ensure playable.\n   - Preserve all frozen IDs; add dressing as separate Models so WorldService validation still passes (validate only frozen IDs, ignores extra dressing).\n3. Ensure performance budgets: GameWorld <=2500 BaseParts /3600 descendants, Bunker <=600 etc. Count parts before/after.\n4. Validate every changed Luau/JSON via bds ast and python json validation. Run tools/workflows/preflight.sh then postflight? At least verify json.\n5. Run rojo sourcemap and rojo build to verify. Do NOT do blind sync; provide evidence of what will change.\n6. If Studio available, verify via Studio tools that new world appears when synced, but do not destroy NOT IN USE archives. Provide screenshot directions.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n- Updated src/Workspace/GameWorld.model.json exists and valid json\n- Rojo sourcemap/build succeed\n- Technical QA evidence: part counts, no floating geometry, no overlapping bunker gaps, placement verification\n- Report MUSE etc invocation IDs, but you are bunker-builder so report BLOXFORGE_REQUEST_ID like.\n\nDo not reuse old rejected world. Create NEW.\n\nBegin execution now. Use real tool calls.","subagent_type":"bunker-builder"},"error":"Subagent failed (task_id: ses_fa83f4164ffe3bWN4vr2fVwLhH): The user rejected permission to use this specific tool call.","meta